cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Unsolved Mathematics Atlas"
message: "If you use this atlas, its formal Lean 4 core, or its meta-analyses, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Donahue"
    given-names: "Alexander S."
    alias: "0thernes"
    email: "0_0@0thernes.art"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8168-9648"
repository-code: "https://github.com/0thernes/unsolved-mathematics"
url: "https://github.com/0thernes/unsolved-mathematics"
abstract: >
  A reproducible, ranked, research-grade dossier collection of 106 open
  mathematical problems across 38 fields, paired with a standalone multi-kernel
  Lean 4.35.0 formal verification core (Collatz structural obstructions and
  epsilon-invariance barrier, Erdős–Straus Mordell mod-840 reduction, Lonely
  Runner sharpness, and Brocard finite verification), automated primary-source
  citation auditing, a deterministic BM25/dense RAG corpus, and documented
  epistemic integrity gates. Human contributions (CRediT): Conceptualization,
  Methodology, Supervision, Formal analysis (statement-fidelity audit),
  Validation, Writing – review & editing. AI tools were used as disclosed
  drafting and formalization instruments; all formal theorems are independently
  checked by Lean 4.35.0 kernels. Not peer-reviewed.
keywords:
  - mathematics
  - open problems
  - conjectures
  - lean4
  - formal verification
  - meta-analysis
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge base
